Task: generic CircuitBreaker.middleware[F, A] (ADR 0010).

Wraps resilience4j-circuitbreaker's core engine as a Guard[F] (see Retry's
note on 57bec6f for why Guard exists). Simpler than
purerest.resilience.CircuitBreaker's HTTP version: no isFailureResult
predicate needed, since a Kafka call has no 'successful-looking value
that's actually a failure' case (no 5xx-as-value equivalent) - uses
resilience4j's onSuccess/onError hooks directly instead of the HTTP
version's value-inspecting onResult. Same CircuitBreakerConfig shape,
same CircuitBreakerOpen exception (no third-party type leaked), same
three metrics (state_transitions counter, calls_rejected counter, state
gauge) under purekafka.circuit_breaker.* instead of purerest.circuit_breaker.*.

Verified: sbt pureKafka/testOnly purekafka.resilience.CircuitBreakerSuite
- 3 passed, 0 failed (stays-closed-while-succeeding, opens-after-threshold-
and-fails-fast, half-open-transition-and-reclose).
